  "readiness": "Useful partial remediation; ordinary supplied regressions and existing guards pass. Correct unconditional immutable-history claims, preserve same-ms and clock-rollback residual as open, then require root review/current-head CI and integration qualification. Not approved here as complete AUD4-F03 closure.",
  "owner_policy_assessment": "Consistent with existing prospective dispute-timeline rule; no new durations, notice classification, ledger semantics, role permission or owner decision is introduced. DEC-012/default counsel questions and A3-F02/DEC-014 remain unresolved. A technical timestamp-history design remains necessary for full immutability; this review does not invent or approve a migration.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "PR87-TIMESTAMP-HISTORY",
      "severity": "Medium retained residual / required documentation correction",
      "locations": [
        "internal/store/sqlite_network.go:71",
        "internal/service/disputes_deadlines.go:20",
        "docs/audit/consolidation-completion-2026-11/AUD4-F03.md:24",
        "docs/audit/consolidation-completion-2026-11/AUD4-F03.md:26"
      ],
      "status": "independently reproduced on candidate production source",
      "mechanism": "The greatest version with effective_at<=OpenedAt can be a policy appended after the dispute when the two operations share a millisecond or host wall time rolls backward. Append-only history does not freeze the selected row.",
      "impact": "The existing test then shows moved deadline, premature overdue reminder, response/waiver bypass and stripped re-review window.",
      "classification": "A remaining portion of the original current-policy bug, not evidence of a newly introduced ledger or authorization regression.",
      "recommendation": "Qualify the source/audit immutability claim, explicitly retain both timestamp conditions as unresolved, and do not describe AUD4-F03 as completely fixed. Any later durable-version/write-order repair requires its own design, tests and review."
    }
  ],
